        "explanation": "<p>Assume $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{A}{x - 1} + \\frac{B}{x + 2}$.<br>Multiply through by $(x - 1)(x + 2)$: $3x + 5 = A(x + 2) + B(x - 1)$.<br>Solve for $A$ and $B$: $A = 2$, $B = 1$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{3x + 5}{(x - 1)(x + 2)} = \\frac{2}{x - 1} + \\frac{1}{x + 2}$.</p>",
