        "question_text": "<p>Find the derivative of $y = x^3 \\ln x$ with respect to $x$.</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Use the product rule: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{d}{dx}(x^3) \\cdot \\ln x + x^3 \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}(\\ln x)$.<br>Thus, $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 3x^2 \\ln x + x^3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{x} = 3x^2 \\ln x + x^2$.</p>",
